---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../layouts/SiteNav.astro";
import { siteUrl } from "../../lib/paths.mjs";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="scat — find the script you need"
  ogDescription="One searchable catalog. A keyboard-first browser. All your scripts, connected."
>
    <header class="masthead">
      <SiteNav />
      <div class="wrap hero">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">
            <span class="status-dot"></span> A little order for your scripts
          </p>
          <h1>Good scripts.<br />Less <em>searching.</em></h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Find the right script, see what it does, and follow what it depends
            on. A shared catalog with a fast CLI and a keyboard-first terminal
            browser.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#setup"
              >Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
            ><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/tjorim/scat"
              >Read the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            >
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">
            Built in Rust <span> / </span> Linux x86-64 <span> / </span> Works
            offline
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual">
          <div class="catalog-label">
            <span>THE SCRIPT CATALOG</span><span>01 / FIND</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="terminal"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Illustrative scat search for backup scripts, showing paths, owners and descriptions"
          >
            <div class="terminal-bar">
              <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span
              ><span>scat — your scripts, connected</span>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal-body">
              <p><span class="prompt">$</span> scat search backup</p>
              <div class="terminal-rule"></div>
              <p class="terminal-heading">PATH <span>OWNER</span></p>
              <p class="terminal-result">ops/backup.sh <span>platform</span></p>
              <p class="terminal-desc">Back up application data</p>
              <p class="terminal-result">
                ops/verify_backup.py <span>platform</span>
              </p>
              <p class="terminal-desc">Check the latest backup</p>
              <p class="terminal-result">lib/storage.py <span>infra</span></p>
              <p class="terminal-desc">Shared storage helpers</p>
              <p class="terminal-foot">
                3 illustrative results
                <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">▊</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="index-tag">
            <span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Discover. Inspect. Connect.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wrap promises">
        <span>One native binary</span><span>Read-only browsing</span
        ><span>No central web service</span
        ><span>No client model downloads</span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <section class="wrap section introduction" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">From “somewhere on the shared drive”</p>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="intro-title">To exactly what<br />you were looking for.</h2>
          <p>
            Scripts accumulate. Context gets lost. Scat brings names, content,
            owners and relationships into one place, without moving your files
            or requiring Git.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="features">
          <article>
            <span class="feature-number">01 / DISCOVER</span>
            <h3>Search beyond the filename.</h3>
            <p>
              Search script content and metadata. Filter by language, owner or
              tag; find function names and declared input or output files.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="feature-number">02 / UNDERSTAND</span>
            <h3>Get the whole picture.</h3>
            <p>
              Preview source, inspect checkout status and compare revisions.
              Follow dependencies, symlinks and related scripts without losing
              your place.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="feature-number">03 / KEEP MOVING</span>
            <h3>Stay in your terminal.</h3>
            <p>
              Browse with the keyboard or use the CLI in your own tools. Export
              selected fields as JSON or search CSV when you need to take
              results further.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section
        id="explore"
        class="explore section"
        aria-labelledby="explore-title"
      >
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">A small catalog. A quick look.</p>
              <h2 id="explore-title">Try finding something.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>
              This browser demo searches a few fictional scripts. The real scat
              searches your indexed files from the CLI or TUI.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="demo">
            <div class="demo-toolbar">
              <label for="query"
                ><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">/</span
                ><input
                  id="query"
                  aria-label="Search sample scripts"
                  type="search"
                  placeholder="Try backup, deploy or storage…"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  spellcheck="false" /></label
              ><span class="demo-badge">SAMPLE CATALOG</span>
            </div>
            <div
              class="demo-filters"
              role="group"
              aria-label="Filter sample scripts by language"
            >
              <button type="button" data-language="all" aria-pressed="true">
                All scripts</button
              ><button type="button" data-language="shell" aria-pressed="false">
                Shell</button
              ><button
                type="button"
                data-language="python"
                aria-pressed="false"
              >
                Python</button
              ><span id="count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="demo-results" id="results"></div>
            <noscript
              ><p class="demo-empty">
                The sample search needs JavaScript. Scat itself runs in your
                terminal; explore its features in the
                <a
                  href={siteUrl("docs/quickstart/")}
                  >quick-start guide</a
                >.
              </p></noscript
            >
            <div class="demo-bottom">
              <code id="command">scat search --limit 50</code
              ><button type="button" id="copy">Copy command</button
              ><span id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="small-note">
            A lightweight illustration, not the scat search engine. The terminal
            app also has full-text ranking, regex search and dependency
            navigation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section
        class="wrap section deployment"
        aria-labelledby="deployment-title"
      >
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Made for shared environments</p>
          <h2 id="deployment-title">
            A shared index.<br />A local experience.
          </h2>
          <p>
            A nightly job builds the SQLite catalog on your indexing host.
            Engineers browse it read-only, with a host-local cache to keep
            ordinary queries off the network share.
          </p>
          <p>
            Built for offline Linux and RHEL workflows. No central web service,
            open ports or runtime language installation needed on clients.
          </p>
          <a
            class="inline-link"
            href={siteUrl("docs/architecture/")}
            >See how it fits together <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <div
          class="flow"
          aria-label="A nightly indexing job publishes a shared catalog, which engineers read through a local cache"
        >
          <div>
            <span class="flow-num">01</span><strong>Indexing host</strong
            ><span>Scan &amp; publish nightly</span>
          </div>
          <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <div>
            <span class="flow-num">02</span><strong>scripts.sqlite</strong
            ><span>One shared catalog</span>
          </div>
          <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <div>
            <span class="flow-num">03</span><strong>Your CLI &amp; TUI</strong
            ><span>Read-only · cached locally</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="setup" class="setup section" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Your next command</p>
          <div class="section-heading">
            <h2 id="setup-title">Get your bearings.</h2>
            <p>
              Start with the Linux x86-64 binary and an existing catalog from
              your team. Publishing a new catalog is a separate administrator
              workflow.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="setup-grid">
            <div>
              <span class="feature-number">01 / GET SCAT</span>
              <h3>Grab a build.</h3>
              <p>
                Download <code>scat-linux-x86_64-musl</code> from a successful
                main-branch run and extract the binary. GitHub may require
                sign-in to download artifacts.
              </p>
              <a
                class="inline-link"
                href="https://github.com/tjorim/scat/actions/workflows/rust-release.yml?query=branch%3Amain"
                >Browse build artifacts ↗</a
              >
              <p class="small-note">
                No tagged releases yet. Optional RPM packaging and site-specific
                installation are covered in the deployment guide.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="feature-number">02 / POINT IT AT YOUR CATALOG</span>
              <pre><code>chmod +x scat
export SCAT_DB=/shared/scripts.sqlite
./scat search backup
./scat tui</code></pre>
              <a
                class="inline-link"
                href={siteUrl("docs/quickstart/")}
                >Read the quick start →</a
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A few useful details</p>
          <h2 id="questions-title">Before you dive in.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <details>
            <summary>Does scat run or change my scripts?</summary>
            <p>
              Ordinary search and browsing read the indexed catalog. Catalog
              builds and vc operations are separate, explicitly invoked
              administrator actions. Opening the TUI does not start an indexer
              or service.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I use it over SSH or without internet access?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. The client reads your catalog offline and supports terminal
              glyph and color overrides for constrained sessions. Clipboard
              forwarding depends on your terminal. See the
              <a
                href={siteUrl("docs/tui-options/#terminal-modes-and-remote-sessions")}
                >SSH and terminal guide</a
              >.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Which systems does it target?</summary>
            <p>
              The main scat binary targets Linux x86-64. RHEL 8, 9 and 10 are
              the intended support matrix, with UBI userspace checks in CI.
              Actual host-policy and mount validation is site-specific; see the
              <a
                href={siteUrl("docs/vendoring/")}
                >deployment guide</a
              >. Windows is not supported by the main client.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Where do I report a problem?</summary>
            <p>
              Run <code>scat doctor</code> for read-only diagnostics, review the
              output for paths and host identifiers before sharing, and
              <a href="https://github.com/tjorim/scat/issues/new"
                >open an issue</a
              >. For command help, run <code>scat --help</code> or press F1 in
              the TUI.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
</SiteLayout>

<script>
  import "../scripts/catalog.js";
</script>
